6. Responsibilities

Engineering Traceability is responsible for:

Recording relationships between engineering artifacts.
Supporting engineering audits.
Enabling engineering verification.
Preserving provenance.
Supporting explainability.
Maintaining accountability throughout engineering cognition.
7. Normative Requirements

Engineering Traceability SHALL:

Preserve relationships between engineering artifacts.
Support forward and backward tracing.
Be maintained throughout engineering cognition.
Support independent verification.
Remain consistent as engineering understanding evolves.

Atlas SHALL NOT produce engineering conclusions that cannot be traced to their supporting evidence and reasoning.

8. Non-Goals

Engineering Traceability does not:

Perform Engineering Reasoning.
Determine Engineering Confidence.
Validate Engineering Evidence.
Replace Engineering Understanding.
Replace Engineering Knowledge.
Authorize engineering decisions.
9. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY define graph-based traceability models, provenance standards, distributed traceability mechanisms, automated impact analysis, and lifecycle auditing techniques without changing the canonical definition established by this specification.